IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 2, ss 8A to 8D -- the Minister's power to have a corporation's books produced,
-- the Magistrate's warrant, copies of books as evidence, and destroying or falsifying a company's documents. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- The Minister, an authorised person and the Magistrate appear only as the holders of powers over the individual; there is no seat for them.
-- The offences (ss 8A(6), 8A(8), 8B(5), 8D(1) and (2)) each have a function that says whether the person is guilty, a function that returns the penalty,
-- and a regulative rule (a duty to comply, or a prohibition derived from the offence under the N2 ruling of 2026-11-04) whose breach path is traced in the tests.
-- Seam (PLAN.md section 4, table A): `s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` answers the keel's input for s 4(8).
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".

§ `Section 8A(1) and (2): the power to require books to be produced`

-- "Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason ... the Minister may at any time" -- a grant gated by "where": the Guide's periods ruling (b) says
-- JUST FALSE when the gate fails (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1 in NOTES.md). The books must be "books relating to the affairs of a corporation".
-- src:2470 | 8A.—(1) Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason
-- src:2471 | for so doing, the Minister may at any time —
-- src:2473 | (a) give directions to a corporation requiring that corporation
-- src:2474 | at such place and time as may be specified in the directions
-- src:2475 | to produce such books relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2476 | corporation as may be so specified; or
-- src:2478 | (b) authorise any person (called in this section and section 8B
-- src:2479 | an authorised person), on producing (if required to do so)
-- src:2480 | evidence of his or her authority, to require that corporation
-- src:2481 | to produce to him or her any books relating to the affairs of
-- src:2482 | a corporation which the authorised person may specify.
@ref s 8A(1) (src:2470-2482)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason for giving the direction or authorising the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the books relate to the affairs of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(1) the Minister has power to require the corporation to produce the books` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason for giving the direction or authorising the person`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason for so doing, the Minister may at any time" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the books relate to the affairs of a corporation`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to require "such books relating to the affairs of a corporation as may be so specified"; the text says nothing of other books

-- src:2484 | (2) Where by virtue of subsection (1) the Minister or an authorised
-- src:2485 | person has power to require the production of any books from a
-- src:2490 | corporation relating to the affairs of a corporation, the Minister or that
-- src:2491 | authorised person has the like power to require production of those
-- src:2492 | books from any person who appears to the Minister or authorised
-- src:2493 | person to be in possession of them; but where any such person claims
-- src:2494 | a lien on any books produced by the person, the production is without
-- src:2495 | prejudice to the lien.
@ref s 8A(2) (src:2484-2495)
GIVEN `the Minister or the authorised person has power under subsection (1) to require the production of the books from a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears to the Minister or the authorised person to be in possession of the books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2) the Minister or the authorised person has the like power to require the person to produce the books` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Minister or the authorised person has power under subsection (1) to require the production of the books from a corporation`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where by virtue of subsection (1) the Minister or an authorised person has power to require the production of any books from a corporation ... the Minister or that authorised person has the like power" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)
    ELSE (IF `the person appears to the Minister or the authorised person to be in possession of the books`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the like power is over "any person who appears to the Minister or authorised person to be in possession of them"; the text says nothing of another person

-- src:2490 | corporation relating to the affairs of a corporation, the Minister or that
-- src:2491 | authorised person has the like power to require production of those
-- src:2492 | books from any person who appears to the Minister or authorised
-- src:2493 | person to be in possession of them; but where any such person claims
-- src:2494 | a lien on any books produced by the person, the production is without
-- src:2495 | prejudice to the lien.
@ref s 8A(2) (src:2490-2495)
GIVEN `the person claims a lien on the books produced by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2) the production of the books is without prejudice to the lien` MEANS
    IF `the person claims a lien on the books produced by the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks only of a person who "claims a lien on any books produced by the person"

§ `Section 8A(3) to (5): what the power includes, what is done with a statement, and who it reaches`

-- src:2497 | (3) Any power conferred by this section to require a corporation or
-- src:2498 | other person to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation
-- src:2499 | includes power —
-- src:2501 | (a) if the books are produced —
-- src:2503 | (i) to make copies of, or take extracts from, them; and
@ref s 8A(3)(a)(i) (src:2497-2503)
GIVEN `the books are produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3)(a)(i) the power includes making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books` MEANS
    IF `the books are produced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes power (a) if the books are produced (i) to make copies of, or take extracts from, them" leaves the power open when the books are not produced

-- src:2497 | (3) Any power conferred by this section to require a corporation or
-- src:2498 | other person to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation
-- src:2499 | includes power —
-- src:2501 | (a) if the books are produced —
-- src:2503 | (i) to make copies of, or take extracts from, them; and
-- src:2505 | (ii) to require that person who is a present or past officer
-- src:2506 | of, or who is or was at any time employed by the
-- src:2507 | corporation to provide an explanation of any of them;
-- src:2508 | and
@ref s 8A(3)(a)(ii) (src:2497-2508)
GIVEN `the books are produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a present or past officer of the corporation, or is or was at any time employed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3)(a)(ii) the power includes requiring the person to provide an explanation of the books` MEANS
    IF `the books are produced` AND `the person is a present or past officer of the corporation, or is or was at any time employed by the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the power "includes" requiring "that person who is a present or past officer of, or who is or was at any time employed by the corporation" to explain the books; the text lists no other person without closing the list

-- src:2497 | (3) Any power conferred by this section to require a corporation or
-- src:2498 | other person to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation
-- src:2499 | includes power —
-- src:2510 | (b) if the books are not produced, to require the person
-- src:2511 | required to produce them to state, to the best of the person’s
-- src:2512 | knowledge and belief, where they are.
@ref s 8A(3)(b) (src:2497-2512)
GIVEN `the books are not produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(3)(b) the power includes requiring the person to state where the books are` MEANS
    IF `the books are not produced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes power ... (b) if the books are not produced, to require the person required to produce them to state, to the best of the person's knowledge and belief, where they are" leaves the power open when the books are produced

-- src:2514 | (4) A statement made by a person in compliance with a requirement
-- src:2515 | imposed by this section may be used in evidence against the person.
@ref s 8A(4) (src:2514-2515)
GIVEN `the statement was made in compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(4) the statement may be used in evidence against the person who made it` MEANS
    IF `the statement was made in compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a statement made by a person in compliance with a requirement imposed by this section"; it says nothing of a statement made otherwise

-- src:2517 | (5) A power conferred by this section to make a requirement of a
-- src:2518 | person extends, if the person is a body corporate (including a body
-- src:2519 | corporate that is in the course of being wound up) or was a body
-- src:2520 | corporate (being a body corporate that has been dissolved) to making
-- src:2521 | that requirement of any person who is or has been an officer of the
-- src:2522 | body corporate.
@ref s 8A(5) (src:2517-2522)
GIVEN `the person on whom the requirement could be made is a body corporate (including one in the course of being wound up) or was a body corporate that has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is or has been an officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(5) the power to make the requirement extends to the individual` MEANS
    IF `the person on whom the requirement could be made is a body corporate (including one in the course of being wound up) or was a body corporate that has been dissolved` AND `the individual is or has been an officer of the body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power "extends ... to making that requirement of any person who is or has been an officer of the body corporate"; the text says nothing of anyone else

§ `Section 8A(6): the offence of not complying, and the defence in (7)`

-- src:2524 | (6) If a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2525 | corporation or provide an explanation or make a statement which is
-- src:2526 | imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation
-- src:2527 | or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty
-- src:2528 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2529 | $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:2530 | both.
@ref s 8A(6) (src:2524-2530)
GIVEN `a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation, or to provide an explanation, or to make a statement, was imposed on the person by virtue of section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation, or to provide an explanation, or to make a statement, was imposed on the person by virtue of section 8A` AND (NOT `the requirement was complied with`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "If a requirement ... imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

-- src:2524 | (6) If a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2525 | corporation or provide an explanation or make a statement which is
-- src:2526 | imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation
-- src:2527 | or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty
-- src:2528 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2529 | $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:2530 | both.
@ref s 8A(6) (src:2524-2530)
GIVEN `a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation, or to provide an explanation, or to make a statement, was imposed on the person by virtue of section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 8A(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 8A(6) the corporation or other person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation, or to provide an explanation, or to make a statement, was imposed on the person by virtue of section 8A` `the requirement was complied with` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 6, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

DECLARE `s 8A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 8A(6) comply with a requirement to produce books, provide an explanation or make a statement`
    `s 8A(8) provide in purported compliance an explanation or statement that is false or misleading in a material particular`

-- The duty a requirement imposes, with the time limit the requirement itself specifies ("at such place and time as may be specified in the directions"):
-- the time is an input, never a number from memory. The consequence the text states is the offence of s 8A(6).
-- src:2473 | (a) give directions to a corporation requiring that corporation
-- src:2474 | at such place and time as may be specified in the directions
-- src:2475 | to produce such books relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2524 | (6) If a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a
-- src:2525 | corporation or provide an explanation or make a statement which is
-- src:2526 | imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation
-- src:2527 | or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty
-- src:2528 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2529 | $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:2530 | both.
@ref s 8A(6) (src:2473-2530)
GIVEN bearer IS A Party
      `the time specified in the requirement, in days after the requirement was imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8A act`
`s 8A(6) the person on whom a requirement was imposed must comply with it` MEANS
    PARTY bearer
    MUST `s 8A(6) comply with a requirement to produce books, provide an explanation or make a statement`
    WITHIN `the time specified in the requirement, in days after the requirement was imposed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY bearer BECAUSE "a requirement imposed by virtue of section 8A was not complied with, which is an offence under section 8A(6)"

-- src:2535 | (7) Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (6)
-- src:2536 | in respect of a requirement to produce any books relating to the affairs
-- src:2537 | of a corporation, it is a defence to prove that they were not in the
-- src:2538 | person’s possession or under the person’s control or that it was not
-- src:2539 | reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement.
@ref s 8A(7) (src:2535-2539)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement was a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the books were not in the person's possession or under the person's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(7) the subsection gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (6)` AND `the requirement was a requirement to produce books relating to the affairs of a corporation`
    THEN (IF    `the person proves that the books were not in the person's possession or under the person's control`
              OR `the person proves that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence to prove that they were not in the person's possession or under the person's control or that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement" -- neither is proved, so this section gives no defence on these facts (the delegated-defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); never "no defence at all"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is charged with an offence under subsection (6) in respect of a requirement to produce any books" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork line F-H-S2)

-- src:2541 | (8) A person, who in purported compliance with a requirement
-- src:2542 | imposed by this section, provides an explanation or statement which
-- src:2543 | the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular or
-- src:2544 | recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is
-- src:2545 | false or misleading in a material particular, shall be guilty of an
-- src:2546 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2547 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2548 | both.
@ref s 8A(8) (src:2541-2548)
GIVEN `the person provided an explanation or statement in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the explanation or statement is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew it to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person provided an explanation or statement in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A`
      AND `the explanation or statement is false or misleading in a material particular`
      AND (`the person knew it to be false or misleading in a material particular` OR `the person was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading in a material particular`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "A person, who in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by this section, provides an explanation or statement which the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular or recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is false or misleading in a material particular, shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- src:2541 | (8) A person, who in purported compliance with a requirement
-- src:2542 | imposed by this section, provides an explanation or statement which
-- src:2543 | the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular or
-- src:2544 | recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is
-- src:2545 | false or misleading in a material particular, shall be guilty of an
-- src:2546 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2547 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2548 | both.
@ref s 8A(8) (src:2541-2548)
GIVEN `the person provided an explanation or statement in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the explanation or statement is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew it to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 8A(8) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 8A(8) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person provided an explanation or statement in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A` `the explanation or statement is false or misleading in a material particular` `the person knew it to be false or misleading in a material particular` `the person was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading in a material particular` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 20000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (N2 ruling of 2026-11-04): the text names the bearer ("A person, who in purported compliance ... provides").
-- src:2541 | (8) A person, who in purported compliance with a requirement
-- src:2542 | imposed by this section, provides an explanation or statement which
-- src:2543 | the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular or
-- src:2544 | recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is
-- src:2545 | false or misleading in a material particular, shall be guilty of an
-- src:2546 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:2547 | $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- src:2548 | both.
@ref s 8A(8) (src:2541-2548)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8A act`
`s 8A(8) a person must not provide a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 8A(8) provide in purported compliance an explanation or statement that is false or misleading in a material particular`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person provided an explanation or statement that is false or misleading in a material particular in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A"

§ `Section 8B: the Magistrate's warrant`

-- "If a Magistrate is satisfied ... the Magistrate may issue a warrant": a grant gated by "if": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1, says NOTHING when the gate fails (fork line F-H-S3).
-- src:2552 | 8B.—(1) If a Magistrate is satisfied, on information on oath or
-- src:2553 | affirmation laid by an authorised person, that there are reasonable
-- src:2554 | grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises any books of
-- src:2555 | which production has been required by virtue of section 8A and
-- src:2556 | which have not been produced in compliance with that requirement,
-- src:2557 | the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising any police officer,
-- src:2558 | together with any other persons named in the warrant, to enter the
-- src:2559 | premises specified in the information (using such force as is
-- src:2560 | reasonably necessary for the purpose) and to search the premises
-- src:2561 | and take possession of any books appearing to be such books or
-- src:2562 | papers as are referred to in this subsection, or to take, in relation to
-- src:2563 | any books so appearing, any other steps which may appear necessary
-- src:2564 | for preserving them and preventing interference with them and to
-- src:2565 | deliver any books, possession of which is so taken, to an authorised
-- src:2566 | person.
@ref s 8B(1) (src:2552-2566)
GIVEN `the information on oath or affirmation was laid by an authorised person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Magistrate is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on the premises books of which production has been required by virtue of section 8A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those books have not been produced in compliance with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(1) the Magistrate may issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter the premises, search them and take possession of the books` MEANS
    IF    `the information on oath or affirmation was laid by an authorised person`
      AND `the Magistrate is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on the premises books of which production has been required by virtue of section 8A`
      AND `those books have not been produced in compliance with that requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the Magistrate may issue a warrant") whose "If" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

-- "continues in force until the end of the period of one month after the date on which it was issued": a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)).
-- src:2568 | (2) Every warrant issued under this section continues in force until
-- src:2569 | the end of the period of one month after the date on which it was
-- src:2570 | issued.
@ref s 8B(2) (src:2568-2570)
GIVEN `the date the warrant was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(2) the warrant is in force on the date asked` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date the warrant was issued` AND `the date asked` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the warrant was issued` 1 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every warrant issued under this section continues in force until the end of the period of one month after the date on which it was issued" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:2572 | (3) Where under this section a person takes possession of, or
-- src:2573 | secures against interference, any books, and a person has a lien on the
-- src:2574 | books, the taking of possession of the books or the securing of the
-- src:2575 | books against interference does not prejudice the lien.
@ref s 8B(3) (src:2572-2575)
GIVEN `a person takes possession of, or secures against interference, books under section 8B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person has a lien on the books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(3) the taking of possession of the books, or the securing of them against interference, prejudices the lien` MEANS
    IF `a person takes possession of, or secures against interference, books under section 8B` AND `a person has a lien on the books`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the taking of possession of the books or the securing of the books against interference does not prejudice the lien" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of books taken or secured under section 8B on which a person has a lien

DECLARE `s 8B(4) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 8B(4)(a) make copies of, or take extracts from, the books`
    `s 8B(4)(b) require a person who was party to the compilation of the books to make a statement providing an explanation`
    `s 8B(4)(c) retain possession of the books for such period as is necessary for their inspection and for copies or extracts to be made by or on behalf of the Minister`

-- "Where, under this section, a person takes possession of, or secures against interference, any books, that person or any authorised person to whose possession the books were delivered -- (a) may ...":
-- a grant gated by "Where": the periods ruling (b) says JUST FALSE when the gate fails (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1).
-- src:2580 | (4) Where, under this section, a person takes possession of, or
-- src:2581 | secures against interference, any books, that person or any authorised
-- src:2582 | person to whose possession the books were delivered —
-- src:2584 | (a) may make copies of, or take extracts from, the books;
-- src:2586 | (b) may require any person who was party to the compilation
-- src:2587 | of the books to make a statement providing any
-- src:2588 | explanation that that person is able to provide as to any
-- src:2589 | matter relating to the compilation of the books or as to any
-- src:2590 | matter to which the books relate;
-- src:2592 | (c) may retain possession of the books for such period as is
-- src:2593 | necessary to enable the books to be inspected, and copies
-- src:2594 | of, or extracts from, the books to be made or taken, by or on
-- src:2595 | behalf of the Minister; and
@ref s 8B(4) (src:2580-2595)
GIVEN power IS A `s 8B(4) power`
      `the person took possession of, or secured against interference, books under section 8B, or is an authorised person to whose possession the books were delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(4) the person has the power` MEANS
    IF `the person took possession of, or secured against interference, books under section 8B, or is an authorised person to whose possession the books were delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, under this section, a person takes possession of, or secures against interference, any books, that person or any authorised person to whose possession the books were delivered -- (a) may make copies ..." (a failed "where" gating a grant: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)

-- src:2597 | (d) during that period must permit a person who would be
-- src:2598 | entitled to inspect any one or more of those books if they
-- src:2599 | were not in the possession of the firstmentioned person to
-- src:2600 | inspect at all reasonable times such of those books as that
-- src:2601 | person would be so entitled to inspect.
@ref s 8B(4)(d) (src:2597-2601)
GIVEN `the books are in the possession of the person who took them, or of an authorised person to whom they were delivered, during the period for which they may be retained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person who would be entitled to inspect one or more of the books if they were not in the possession of the firstmentioned person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the person entitled to inspect to inspect the books at all reasonable times` MEANS
    IF `the books are in the possession of the person who took them, or of an authorised person to whom they were delivered, during the period for which they may be retained` AND `the person is a person who would be entitled to inspect one or more of the books if they were not in the possession of the firstmentioned person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during that period must permit a person who would be entitled to inspect any one or more of those books if they were not in the possession of the firstmentioned person to inspect at all reasonable times such of those books as that person would be so entitled to inspect" -- the duty arises only for such a person during that period (a duty whose gate is unmet: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- src:2603 | (5) A person who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search
-- src:2604 | conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section, or who
-- src:2605 | obstructs the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any
-- src:2606 | books, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:2607 | to a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:2608 | exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 8B(5) (src:2603-2608)
GIVEN `the person obstructed the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under section 8B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obstructed the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person obstructed the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under section 8B` OR `the person obstructed the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "A person who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section, or who obstructs the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books, shall be guilty of an offence" -- neither element is met

-- src:2603 | (5) A person who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search
-- src:2604 | conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section, or who
-- src:2605 | obstructs the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any
-- src:2606 | books, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:2607 | to a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:2608 | exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 8B(5) (src:2603-2608)
GIVEN `the person obstructed the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under section 8B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obstructed the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 8B(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 8B(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person obstructed the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under section 8B` `the person obstructed the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any books` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 6, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

DECLARE `s 8B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 8B(5) obstruct the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by a warrant, or the exercise of a right to take possession of any books`
    `s 8B(4)(d) permit a person entitled to inspect the books to inspect them at all reasonable times`

-- src:2603 | (5) A person who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search
-- src:2604 | conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section, or who
-- src:2605 | obstructs the exercise of a right so conferred to take possession of any
-- src:2606 | books, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:2607 | to a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:2608 | exceeding 6 months or to both.
@ref s 8B(5) (src:2603-2608)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8B act`
`s 8B(5) a person must not obstruct a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 8B(5) obstruct the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by a warrant, or the exercise of a right to take possession of any books`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person obstructed the exercise of a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant issued under section 8B"

-- The duty of s 8B(4)(d): a MUST with no time limit and no consequence the text states (no breach path).
-- src:2597 | (d) during that period must permit a person who would be
-- src:2598 | entitled to inspect any one or more of those books if they
-- src:2599 | were not in the possession of the firstmentioned person to
-- src:2600 | inspect at all reasonable times such of those books as that
-- src:2601 | person would be so entitled to inspect.
@ref s 8B(4)(d) (src:2597-2601)
GIVEN `the name of the person in possession` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8B act`
`s 8B(4)(d) the person in possession must permit the inspection` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person in possession`
    MUST `s 8B(4)(d) permit a person entitled to inspect the books to inspect them at all reasonable times`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 8B(4)(d) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person in possession` BECAUSE "the person in possession did not permit a person entitled to inspect the books to inspect them" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:2610 | (6) The powers conferred by this section are in addition to, and not
-- src:2611 | in derogation of, any other power conferred by law.
@ref s 8B(6) (src:2610-2611)
GIVEN `the other power is a power conferred by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8B(6) the powers conferred by section 8B derogate from the other power` MEANS
    IF `the other power is a power conferred by law`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The powers conferred by this section are in addition to, and not in derogation of, any other power conferred by law" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of other powers conferred by law

§ `Section 8C: copies of or extracts from books as evidence`

-- (1) and (2) together: "Subject to this section ... admissible ... as if it were the original"; "not admissible ... unless it is proved that the copy or extract is a true copy".
-- src:2615 | 8C.—(1) Subject to this section, in any legal proceedings, whether
-- src:2616 | proceedings under this Act or otherwise, a copy of or extract from a
-- src:2617 | book relating to the affairs of a corporation is admissible in evidence
-- src:2618 | as if it were the original book or the relevant part of the original book.
-- src:2620 | (2) A copy of or extract from a book is not admissible in evidence
-- src:2621 | under subsection (1) unless it is proved that the copy or extract is a
-- src:2622 | true copy of the book or of the relevant part of the book.
@ref s 8C(1) (src:2615-2622)
GIVEN `the proceedings are legal proceedings, whether proceedings under this Act or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy or extract is a copy of or extract from a book relating to the affairs of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the copy or extract is a true copy of the book or of the relevant part of the book` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8C(1) and (2) the copy or extract is admissible in evidence as if it were the original book or the relevant part of it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are legal proceedings, whether proceedings under this Act or otherwise` AND `the copy or extract is a copy of or extract from a book relating to the affairs of a corporation`
    THEN (IF `it is proved that the copy or extract is a true copy of the book or of the relevant part of the book`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of or extract from a book is not admissible in evidence under subsection (1) unless it is proved that the copy or extract is a true copy of the book or of the relevant part of the book" (a flat negative with an "unless")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "any legal proceedings" and of "a copy of or extract from a book relating to the affairs of a corporation"; the text says nothing of any other copy

DECLARE `s 8C(3) way of giving the evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 8C(3) orally`
    `s 8C(3) by an affidavit sworn before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations`
    `s 8C(3) by a declaration made before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations`
    `s 8C(3) in some other way`

-- src:2627 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), evidence that a copy of or
-- src:2628 | extract from a book is a true copy of the book or of a part of the book
-- src:2629 | may be given by a person who has compared the copy or extract with
-- src:2630 | the book or the relevant part of the book and may be given either
-- src:2631 | orally or by an affidavit sworn, or by a declaration made, before a
-- src:2632 | person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations.
-- src:2634 | Destruction, mutilation, etc., of company documents
@ref s 8C(3) (src:2627-2634)
GIVEN `the evidence is given by a person who has compared the copy or extract with the book or the relevant part of the book` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `s 8C(3) way of giving the evidence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8C(3) the evidence is evidence that the copy or extract is a true copy` MEANS
    IF `the evidence is given by a person who has compared the copy or extract with the book or the relevant part of the book`
    THEN (CONSIDER way
          WHEN `s 8C(3) orally` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 8C(3) by an affidavit sworn before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 8C(3) by a declaration made before a person authorised to take affidavits or statutory declarations` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the evidence "may be given either orally or by an affidavit sworn, or by a declaration made, before a person authorised"; the text says nothing of another way
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the evidence "may be given by a person who has compared the copy or extract with the book"; the text says nothing of evidence from a person who has not

§ `Section 8D: destroying, mutilating or falsifying company documents`

-- src:2654 | (4) In this section, “officer of a corporation” includes a person
-- src:2655 | who —
-- src:2657 | (a) was at any time an officer of the corporation; or
-- src:2659 | (b) has, or had, a financial or other interest in the affairs of the
-- src:2660 | corporation.
@ref s 8D(4) (src:2654-2660)
GIVEN `the person was at any time an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has, or had, a financial or other interest in the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8D(4) the person is within the words officer of a corporation` MEANS
    IF `the person was at any time an officer of the corporation` OR `the person has, or had, a financial or other interest in the affairs of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, 'officer of a corporation' includes a person who (a) was at any time an officer of the corporation; or (b) has, or had, a financial or other interest" leaves the term open

-- src:2636 | 8D.—(1) An officer of a corporation to which section 8A(1)
-- src:2637 | applies, who destroys, mutilates or falsifies, or is privy to the
-- src:2638 | destruction, mutilation or falsification of a document affecting or
-- src:2639 | relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or makes or is
-- src:2640 | privy to the making of a false entry in such a document, shall, unless
-- src:2641 | the officer proves that he or she had no intention to conceal the affairs
-- src:2642 | of the corporation or to defeat the law, be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 8D(1) (src:2636-2642)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the corporation, as subsection (4) uses the words` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 8A(1) applies to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroyed, mutilated or falsified a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or was privy to its destruction, mutilation or falsification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made, or was privy to the making of, a false entry in such a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the person had no intention to conceal the affairs of the corporation or to defeat the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8D(1) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an officer of the corporation, as subsection (4) uses the words`
      AND `section 8A(1) applies to the corporation`
      AND (   `the person destroyed, mutilated or falsified a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or was privy to its destruction, mutilation or falsification`
           OR `the person made, or was privy to the making of, a false entry in such a document`)
      AND (NOT `the person proves that the person had no intention to conceal the affairs of the corporation or to defeat the law`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2, and an "unless" met): "An officer of a corporation to which section 8A(1) applies, who destroys, mutilates or falsifies ... shall, unless the officer proves that he or she had no intention to conceal the affairs of the corporation or to defeat the law, be guilty of an offence"

-- src:2644 | (2) A person to whom subsection (1) applies who fraudulently
-- src:2645 | either parts with, alters or makes an omission in any such document,
-- src:2646 | or who is privy to fraudulent parting with, fraudulent altering or
-- src:2647 | fraudulent making of an omission in, any such document, shall be
-- src:2648 | guilty of an offence.
@ref s 8D(2) (src:2644-2648)
GIVEN `the person is a person to whom subsection (1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fraudulently parted with, altered or made an omission in such a document, or was privy to its fraudulent parting with, fraudulent altering or the fraudulent making of an omission in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8D(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person to whom subsection (1) applies` AND `the person fraudulently parted with, altered or made an omission in such a document, or was privy to its fraudulent parting with, fraudulent altering or the fraudulent making of an omission in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line F-H-S2): "A person to whom subsection (1) applies who fraudulently either parts with, alters or makes an omission in any such document ... shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- (3) the penalty for an offence under either subsection.
-- src:2650 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section shall be liable
-- src:2651 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for
-- src:2652 | a term not exceeding 2 years or to both.
@ref s 8D(3) (src:2650-2652)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under section 8D(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 8D(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under section 8D(1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for "A person guilty of an offence under this section"

DECLARE `s 8D act` IS ONE OF
    `s 8D(1) destroy, mutilate or falsify a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or make a false entry in it`
    `s 8D(2) fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in such a document`

-- src:2636 | 8D.—(1) An officer of a corporation to which section 8A(1)
-- src:2637 | applies, who destroys, mutilates or falsifies, or is privy to the
-- src:2638 | destruction, mutilation or falsification of a document affecting or
-- src:2639 | relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or makes or is
-- src:2640 | privy to the making of a false entry in such a document, shall, unless
-- src:2641 | the officer proves that he or she had no intention to conceal the affairs
-- src:2642 | of the corporation or to defeat the law, be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 8D(1) (src:2636-2642)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8D act`
`s 8D(1) an officer must not destroy, mutilate or falsify a company document, or make a false entry in it` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 8D(1) destroy, mutilate or falsify a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or make a false entry in it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer destroyed, mutilated or falsified a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation, or made a false entry in it"

-- src:2644 | (2) A person to whom subsection (1) applies who fraudulently
-- src:2645 | either parts with, alters or makes an omission in any such document,
-- src:2646 | or who is privy to fraudulent parting with, fraudulent altering or
-- src:2647 | fraudulent making of an omission in, any such document, shall be
-- src:2648 | guilty of an offence.
@ref s 8D(2) (src:2644-2648)
GIVEN `the name of the officer` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 8D act`
`s 8D(2) a person must not fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in a company document` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer`
    SHANT `s 8D(2) fraudulently part with, alter or make an omission in such a document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer` BECAUSE "the officer fraudulently parted with, altered or made an omission in a document affecting or relating to the property or affairs of the corporation"

-- The seam of PLAN.md section 4, table A: s 4(8) of the keel asks `the reference is in section 8A, 8C, 8D, 216, Part 9 or section 402`.
-- This part answers for the three sections that are its own; the other three are other parts' and answer NOTHING here.
-- src:2470 | 8A.—(1) Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason
-- src:2615 | 8C.—(1) Subject to this section, in any legal proceedings, whether
-- src:2636 | 8D.—(1) An officer of a corporation to which section 8A(1)
@ref s 8A (src:2470-2636)
GIVEN `the section in which the reference appears` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8A, 8C and 8D the reference is in section 8A, 8C or 8D` MEANS
    IF    `the section in which the reference appears` EQUALS "8A"
       OR `the section in which the reference appears` EQUALS "8C"
       OR `the section in which the reference appears` EQUALS "8D"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): sections 216, 402 and Part 9 are other parts' provisions, and every other section is outside the list s 4(8) names
